# House style

<!--
Optional, opt-in resume-writing guidance.

Copy this file to config/style_guide.md to activate it. Its prose is appended
to the system message of every resume tailor-loop agent: writer, reviser, and
reviewers. The block is appended beneath the fixed fact-lock rules.

It governs how your resume is written: tone, emphasis, ordering, structure, and
industry conventions. It cannot introduce facts. Every claim still has to trace
to data/profile/facts.json, and the fact-check gate is unchanged.

Delete this comment and write freely below. Missing or empty file = no change.
-->

Write in a crisp, results-first register suitable for senior software roles.

- Lead every experience bullet with a quantified outcome, then the action.
- Prefer strong verbs like built, shipped, and scaled.
- Foreground systems and infrastructure work for backend roles.
- Keep it to one page; cut hobby projects unless they show a required skill.
- Use American spelling and the Oxford comma.
